.TH "RAUC" "1" "Mar 28, 2026" "1.15.2" "RAUC"
.SH "نام (NAME)"
rauc \- safe and secure updating
.SH "خلاصه دستور (SYNOPSIS)"
.sp
\fBrauc\fP [\fIOPTIONS\fP\&...] \fBbundle\fP \fIINPUTDIR\fP \fIBUNDLE\fP
.sp
\fBrauc\fP [\fIOPTIONS\fP\&...] \fBresign\fP \fIINBUNDLE\fP \fIOUTBUNDLE\fP
.sp
\fBrauc\fP [\fIOPTIONS\fP\&...] \fBextract\fP \fIBUNDLE\fP \fIOUTPUTDIR\fP
.sp
\fBrauc\fP [\fIOPTIONS\fP\&...] \fBextract\-signature\fP \fIBUNDLE\fP \fIOUTPUTSIG\fP
.sp
\fBrauc\fP [\fIOPTIONS\fP\&...] \fBconvert\fP \fIINBUNDLE\fP \fIOUTBUNDLE\fP
.sp
\fBrauc\fP [\fIOPTIONS\fP\&...] \fBencrypt\fP \fIINBUNDLE\fP \fIOUTBUNDLE\fP
.sp
\fBrauc\fP [\fIOPTIONS\fP\&...] \fBinstall\fP \fIBUNDLE\fP
.sp
\fBrauc\fP [\fIOPTIONS\fP\&...] \fBinfo\fP \fIBUNDLE\fP
.sp
\fBrauc\fP [\fIOPTIONS\fP\&...] \fBmount\fP \fIBUNDLE\fP
.sp
\fBrauc\fP [\fIOPTIONS\fP\&...] \fBstatus\fP [\fISLOTNAME\fP |
\fBmark\-\fP{\fBgood\fP,\fBbad\fP,\fBactive\fP}
[\fBbooted\fP|\fBother\fP|\fISLOTNAME\fP]]
.sp
\fBrauc\fP [\fIOPTIONS\fP\&...] \fBwrite\-slot\fP \fISLOTNAME\fP \fIIMAGEFILE\fP
.SH "توضیحات (DESCRIPTION)"
.sp
RAUC is a lightweight update client that runs on an Embedded Linux
device and reliably controls the procedure of updating the device with a
new firmware.
.sp
RAUC is also the tool on the host system that is used to create, inspect
and modify update files (\(dqbundles\(dq) for the device.
.sp
This manual page documents briefly the \fBrauc\fP command line utility.
.sp
It was written for the Debian GNU/Linux distribution to satisfy the
packaging requirements. Thus it should only serve as a summary, reading
the comprehensive online manual (\fBhttps://rauc.readthedocs.io/\fP) is
recommended.
.SH "گزینه‌ها (OPTIONS)"
.sp
The following general options can be used with most commands, however
not all combinations make sense.
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
\fB\-c\fP \fIFILENAME\fP, \fB\-\-conf=\fP\fIFILENAME\fP
use the given config file instead of the one at the compiled\-in
default path
.TP
\fB\-C\fP \fISECTION:KEY=VALUE\fP, \fB\-\-confopt=\fP\fISECTION:KEY=VALUE\fP
Override parameters from the config file with the specified
configuration settings. If specified parameter is not present in the
config file it will still be set by this option.
.TP
\fB\-\-keyring=\fP\fIPEMFILE\fP
use specific keyring file
.TP
\fB\-\-mount=\fP\fIPATH\fP
mount prefix (/mnt/rauc by default)
.TP
\fB\-d\fP, \fB\-\-debug\fP
enable debug output
.TP
\fB\-\-version\fP
display version
.TP
\fB\-h\fP, \fB\-\-help\fP
print usage
.UNINDENT
.SH COMMANDS
.sp
\fBbundle\fP \fIINPUTDIR\fP \fIBUNDLE\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
Create a bundle from a content directory.
.sp
\fBOptions:\fP
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
